From 3e4692984a2d6853c0c9edd068bf90fbcddbb0f4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jgrizon
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 15:06:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] shader: lane-alike branches run together; scalar inputs are
 per wave

A branch on a lane condition the console wave holds alike splits the two host
waves no more than a scalar one, so in_step now treats it as running together
where halves::lane_uniform knows the condition is one value per console wave.
lane_uniform also seeds the scalar inputs (user data, system values; not EXEC
or VCC) as one value per wave. That lets the halves hand a first lane, a lane
read or a reduction over exactly instead of answering from the reader's half,
and lets barrier placement see such loops as in step. lane_uniform is computed
once and shared by the barrier and halves paths.

This is the remaining half of the first-lane refusals VICTORY_WAVE_WHY
attributed to loop counts and indices computed by vector float math.

Ported from paveledits/ScarlettMac runtime-preview/checkpoint/patches/0011-shader-lane-alike-branches-run-together-scalar-input.patch

